{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas","id":1141469,"title":"September Update: Check out the Devas!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-18T11:20:32-07:00","id":1141469,"title":"September Update: Check out the Devas!","content":"Ok, so, short overview first : I freaking love the Deva write-up overall... there may be a few points where initial reading made me go a little 'whu?' but the more I read it the more I find I love it and find that Mendez has done an amazing job with the Hindu Pantheon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, for the longer review : I love the introduction. Both for how utterly badass the second paragraph makes the Pantheon sound and also because the beginning paragraph is emulating the Nasadiya Suktam, the Vedic Hymn of Creation.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to see Kartikkeya included, and pretty ecstatic to see Durga (and not as an aka of Kali). Speaking of whom, I am just a tad dissapointed that Kali isn't in the core... I hope to see her in the Companion, and I'll probably put up my own homebrew write-up for her in a bit for all the potential Annie X's out there.<br /> <br /> As a Shakta myself, I love the references to how the Goddesses are constantly splitting and fusing with each other.<br /> <br /> As for the actual God writeups, I'm particularly fond of the way the introductory paragraphs manage to stuff in half a dozen origin stories in the style of a hymn. I'm particularly fond of the write-ups for Durga, Ganesha and, most of all, Sarasvati (the last of which basically makes me want to create a Scion of Her right now). Also, love the inclusion of Indra's entire menagerie and the opening line for Shiva is pretty much the most Shiva sentence ever.<br /> <br /> I'm also happy to see the wide variety of opinions... while the Deva are as a whole undoubtedly among the most dedicated to opposing the Titans, for every Durga and Indra we see an Agni and a Ganesha, and yet others like Parvati, Sarasvati and Lakshmi, who seem more interested in just helping people out than any war.<br /> <br /> Cosmology wise I love the Sixteen Planes of Existence (which I'm sure is another thing the Deva love hanging over the Aesir and their Nine Worlds)... the description of the Cow Level and the Mani Continent makes me imagine Krishna and Durga literally trying to jostle each other's realms out of top like a pair of drivers in a high octane car chase sequence in some action movie.<br /> <br /> I am a little iffy on Brahma being a Primordial... not that he doesn't fit the bill honestly, but it makes him feel a little out of sync with Vishnu and Shiva (which, again, to be fair, is not unfitting his actual treatment in the religion). Basically I feel there's more than one right answer to the Brahma question and I think Mendez' position is most definitely one of those right answers.<br /> <br /> Fun Fact : While I am a Kshatriya by caste, my specific sub-caste is Kayastha, whose traditional task has been governance and most importantly, scribe-work. The whole line is supposedly descended from Chitragupta, the scribe-scretary of Yama, so it's actually kinda funny for me to see my supposed mythical divine ancestor mentioned in the Naraka write-up.<br /> <br /> I am very happy that in the World the Island Kingdom of Lanka is explicitly different from the actual country of Sri Lanka... from what I gather Sri Lankans aren't very happy with being told that their country used to be ruled by Titans until an Indian Prince came and saved them, so good call I think.<br /> <br /> I will give Mendez seven stars for his write-up just for calling the Religion Section 'The Hinduisms' instead of Hinduism <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It is an excellent overview of the religions(s) and I love how it emphasizes the inherent crazy amounts of diversity in it.<br /> <br /> Rounding up, the Birthrights part and current political situation is very good, and I've already noted how perfectly fitting I think the Virtues of Conscience and Duty and the PSP of Yoga is.<br /> <br /> I think one of the best compliments I can give the Deva write up is actually something Sacredos said way back when the Shen were previewed... &quot;All together, I think this is the most well-crafted Pantheon yet, it really gives off the feel you get from reading traditional Chinese literature.&quot;<br /> <br /> And truly, reading this gives me the feel of reading scripture, with the sheer reverence that went into the God profiles and the description of the World of the Deva... and the impact the Deva have upon the World... Great job! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, full disclosure, I had the good fortune of being one of the Beta Readers mentioned in the update, so I've been sitting on my gushing for a while now, and I'm happy to finally see it come out to the World <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T11:50:40-07:00","id":1141477,"title":"","content":"Hey Samudra,Remember Rishis storyes you told me? This preview makes them even more awesome,since it means that Brahma,the <i>primordial</i> was turned into a baby by Atri and Cursed by Bhrigu,That's just Awesome in spades","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:02:32-07:00","id":1141481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas#post1141469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a little iffy on Brahma being a Primordial... not that he doesn't fit the bill honestly, but it makes him feel a little out of sync with Vishnu and Shiva (which, again, to be fair, is not unfitting his actual treatment in the religion). Basically I feel there's more than one right answer to the Brahma question and I think Mendez' position is most definitely one of those right answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I think makes it make sense (I was thinking about it because I had similar initial feelings as you), is that it's been implied that in Scion 2E a deity's exact state between Primordial, Titan, and God can shift. Vishnu and Shiva are Gods BECAUSE they chose to be more engaged with their worshipers and/or incarnate more directly into the world; while Brahma chooses to remain more distant and transcendent in identity and thus remains a Primordial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:10:22-07:00","id":1141483,"title":"","content":"Obviously hoping to see Kali in the Scion Companion. My other top pick for a deity not on this list currently would be <b><i>Chandra</i></b>. She's less important today under the the paradigms of Vaishnavaism, Shaivism, and Shaktism - but in the older Vedic tradition she'd be the lunar counterpart to Surya's solar dominion, in addition to being an astrology goddess, and the goddess of soma itself (giving her a role not unlike Idunn for the Aesir).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:44:44-07:00","id":1141493,"title":"","content":"As with all the other pantheon preview before, i really like the part about the pantheons relationship with the other pantheons. And again, as with the other previews, i would've wish to see more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:50:11-07:00","id":1141496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas#post1141469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the actual God writeups, I'm particularly fond of the way the introductory paragraphs manage to stuff in half a dozen origin stories in the style of a hymn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both fitting the tone, AND acknowledging &quot;Look there's like SIX different stories about where Ganesha came from&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: I also like the note in the Relic section that says &quot;Look, the Deva have a HUGE amount of awe-inspiring superweapons&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-18-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T13:20:45-07:00","id":1141515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141496#post1141496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: I also like the note in the Relic section that says &quot;Look, the Deva have a HUGE amount of awe-inspiring superweapons&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting that supposedly no wielder of another pantheon's superweapons want to test their might against the astra - because I'd think someone suggesting that was the case would just make Thor grab Mjolnir and scream &quot;CHALLENGE ACCEPTED!&quot;<br /> <br /> I realize of course that elsewhere its states both Pantheons work to make sure Thor and Indra don't run into each other... but honestly that would just make Loki scream &quot;CHALLENGE ACCEPTED!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:03:32-07:00","id":1141532,"title":"","content":"So thinking about their legends - I'm assuming the Anunna are also in the hardline-Titanomachy camp with the Deva, Teotl, and the Theoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:13:54-07:00","id":1141537,"title":"","content":"And that's the hook for someone's campaign.<br /> Echoing all the praise so far, the only thing I could even come close to campaigning about is curiosity about why Kali wasn't in? I guess there's probably some work to do separating pop culture and original myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:28:26-07:00","id":1141543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141532#post1141532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So thinking about their legends - I'm assuming the Anunna are also in the hardline-Titanomachy camp with the Deva, Teotl, and the Theoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know what Annuna related matter i'm really curious about? Their Tablet that controls fate,how does such a relic work in the Scion World i wonder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:53:02-07:00","id":1141549,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes the Deva. There isn't really much I can say that wasn't already said by the opening post, but I do enjoy how closely it is correlated with Vedic texts. Admittedly, I am somewhat jealous how well this reads in comparison to the previous Shen preview, although I think it is partly because some translations of Chinese texts, particularly of the local variety, just don't exist and so can't be referenced.<br /> <br /> But if they can keep up this amount of quality up for the Kami preview once that becomes available, I will be quite satisfied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T15:13:06-07:00","id":1141556,"title":"","content":"There's also the unavoidable reality that Scion's default cosmological assumptions do emerge from an Indo-European tradition (hence the Titanomachy being the degree of &quot;thing&quot; it is), so even when writers do a great job with the Shen or Netjer or Orisha there's a degree to which they are crammed to fit a paradigm that the Deva (particularly the older Vedic gods) more easily slip into.<br /> <br /> Without question though 2E is doing a WAY better job with it than 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T15:58:28-07:00","id":1141569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141483#post1141483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously hoping to see Kali in the Scion Companion. My other top pick for a deity not on this list currently would be <b><i>Chandra</i></b>. She's less important today under the the paradigms of Vaishnavaism, Shaivism, and Shaktism - but in the older Vedic tradition she'd be the lunar counterpart to Surya's solar dominion, in addition to being an astrology goddess, and the goddess of soma itself (giving her a role not unlike Idunn for the Aesir).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping to put up a homebrew of Kali in a day or so actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> also while I love Chandra, I've never seen him depicted as a Goddess, always a God. My other pick for inclusion in the Companion would be Ganga, Goddess of the Sacred Ganges River, who no doubt has... Words to say about the current state of said river <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:23:49-07:00","id":1141580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141481#post1141481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that I think makes it make sense (I was thinking about it because I had similar initial feelings as you), is that it's been implied that in Scion 2E a deity's exact state between Primordial, Titan, and God can shift. Vishnu and Shiva are Gods BECAUSE they chose to be more engaged with their worshipers and/or incarnate more directly into the world; while Brahma chooses to remain more distant and transcendent in identity and thus remains a Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, depending on whom you ask, Brahma's lack of worship is a side effect of being cursed by either his wife Sarasvati or his brother-in-law Shiva... (which I guess is a God level Artistry marvel, to literally change the course of culture to the point where a God is no longer worshipped commonly) which would mean Brahma becoming (or staying, depending on how you think he started out) a Primordial is on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:30:31-07:00","id":1141583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141569#post1141569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping to put up a homebrew of Kali in a day or so actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> also while I love Chandra, I've never seen him depicted as a Goddess, always a God. My other pick for inclusion in the Companion would be Ganga, Goddess of the Sacred Ganges River, who no doubt has... Words to say about the current state of said river <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oops! My mistake and apologies. I had misremembered what I was taught on the subject. I had no doubt you were correct, but checking my ow notes the error was definitely my own memory rather than my sources. So again, my mistake!<br /> <br /> I think I made the mistake because all the cases I know of it being a personal name are of women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-18-2017, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:38:02-07:00","id":1141586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141580#post1141580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, depending on whom you ask, Brahma's lack of worship is a side effect of being cursed by either his wife Sarasvati or his brother-in-law Shiva... (which I guess is a God level Artistry marvel, to literally change the course of culture to the point where a God is no longer worshipped commonly) which would mean Brahma becoming (or staying, depending on how you think he started out) a Primordial is on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is an interesting inversion in Scion of what seems to have happened with the Netjer, where Aset stealing Re's True Name allowed him to be bound in a more definable nature of godhood (hence the first being who is the progenitor of 2 generations of Primordials being a God, and historically that first being's relatively late emergence in Egyptian worship)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:46:25-07:00","id":1141588,"title":"","content":"Samudra, I'm curious as to your opinion on future inclusion of Lord Hanuman. Should he be a distinct deity in his own right, an Avatar of Shiva in the way Rama is an Avatar of Vishnu, or perhaps a Demigod level Scion of the Wind God Vayu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T17:08:17-07:00","id":1141590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141588#post1141588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Samudra, I'm curious as to your opinion on future inclusion of Lord Hanuman. Should he be a distinct deity in his own right, an Avatar of Shiva in the way Rama is an Avatar of Vishnu, or perhaps a Demigod level Scion of the Wind God Vayu?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Hanuman has enough chops to be a God in his own right, though the Preview does treat Him as an Avatara/Mantle of Shiva (hence the Beasts(Monkeys)). Hanuman is one of the most widely worshipped deities in Hinduism, with a popularity rivaling Ganesh for cross sectarian popularity, and he arguably also eclipses Rama in popularity (which should surprise no one really, how many people remember that Monkey isn't the protagonist of Journey to the West). Either of the first two options you mention, I think, would work for him... And given how who is a mantle of whom can get very confusing very fast among the Deva (especially among the goddesses), I'd say they could both be true at the same time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T19:13:55-07:00","id":1141621,"title":"","content":"I wanted to thank <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> again for invaluable help with the writing process.<br /> <br /> Re: Brahma: His Primordial status definitely reflects current trends in worship. Like Xiwangmu, in many historical settings prior to his retirement, he'd probably be a straight-up God.<br /> <br /> Re: Kali: We gotta keep <b>something</b> good in reserve for the Companion. ~_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T21:13:33-07:00","id":1141650,"title":"","content":"Pantheon writeup: Rad.<br /> <br /> Desire to make a Deva scion: Piqued.<br /> <br /> Now currently reading: Ramayana.<br /> <br /> Writeup Mission: Accomplished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T23:04:07-07:00","id":1141668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141556#post1141556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the unavoidable reality that Scion's default cosmological assumptions do emerge from an Indo-European tradition (hence the Titanomachy being the degree of &quot;thing&quot; it is), so even when writers do a great job with the Shen or Netjer or Orisha there's a degree to which they are crammed to fit a paradigm that the Deva (particularly the older Vedic gods) more easily slip into.<br /> <br /> Without question though 2E is doing a WAY better job with it than 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think they have been firmly doing away with those assumptions, and quite a few other pantheons don't subscribe to that point of view, The Orisha being a good example of this. Indeed it seems the farther away one gets from the middle land mass (i.e. West Asia, Northeast Africa, and Southeast Europe), the more likely the mythology doesn't subscribe to the paradigm of titanomachy from the previews we have gotten so far. What should be telling is what the Teotl and Kami think about it, since they think in a very different way to the Orisha and their priorities and thought process has not been revealed so far. I would guess that the Kami are in a similar position as the Shen regarding their alliance with the Deva but agreeing in principle with the Orisha point of view. But the Teotl I couldn't guess at.<br /> <br /> But the reality is that there are linguistic limitations when attempting to portray the Netjer, Shen, and Teotl because their is just not enough English material on them to reference or use. There are a lot of Chinese texts on local gods that I know of that the writers could probably never reference since their is no English translation of it. I actually fear that the Kami may be interpreted in an animistic way as defined by Western scholars, but I hope that is not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 09-19-2017, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T23:25:51-07:00","id":1141670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141668#post1141668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Teotl I couldn't guess at.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deva Preview actually gives us a pretty good idea of that... it states that the Deva get along with them very well because they both have hardline stances on the Titanomachy. I'm pretty sure Lula gave us a rundown of the various Pantheons' attitudes towards Titans and the Deva and Teotl are pretty much at the top of the 'in favour' list. The Kami are mysteriously missing from that rundown though, so no idea what they subscribe to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T23:27:49-07:00","id":1141671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141621#post1141621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to thank <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> again for invaluable help with the writing process.<br /> <br /> Re: Brahma: His Primordial status definitely reflects current trends in worship. Like Xiwangmu, in many historical settings prior to his retirement, he'd probably be a straight-up God.<br /> <br /> Re: Kali: We gotta keep <b>something</b> good in reserve for the Companion. ~_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm looking forward to what you do with the Deva in the Companion, and thank you again for the great job portraying my rl Gods. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:05:14-07:00","id":1141675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141670#post1141670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Deva Preview actually gives us a pretty good idea of that... it states that the Deva get along with them very well because they both have hardline stances on the Titanomachy. I'm pretty sure Lula gave us a rundown of the various Pantheons' attitudes towards Titans and the Deva and Teotl are pretty much at the top of the 'in favour' list. The Kami are mysteriously missing from that rundown though, so no idea what they subscribe to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed that, though I suspect its probably different from their side.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see it mentions belligerence but not necessarily titanomachy, I guess we shall see later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 09-19-2017, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:26:46-07:00","id":1141680,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something but why are the Devas so hard on the Yazatas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:33:00-07:00","id":1141684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141680#post1141680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something but why are the Devas so hard on the Yazatas?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand there's many many years of real-world conflict that's led to a LOT of bad blood between the two cultures and myths of old.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I am not an expert in anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:40:58-07:00","id":1141685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141684#post1141684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand there's many many years of real-world conflict that's led to a LOT of bad blood between the two cultures and myths of old.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I am not an expert in anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The conflict's beginning is described under Current Priorities - the Asuras/Ahuras eventually became the Yazata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T02:02:42-07:00","id":1141688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141680#post1141680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something but why are the Devas so hard on the Yazatas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahura - Asura<br /> <br /> Daeva - Deva<br /> <br /> Both pantheons have been counting the other among their Titans for millennia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T05:19:19-07:00","id":1141711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141675#post1141675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must have missed that, though I suspect its probably different from their side.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see it mentions belligerence but not necessarily titanomachy, I guess we shall see later.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most general terms the Deva, Teotl, and Theoi are the Titanomachy hardliners, with the Deva as the groups' self-assumed leadership.<br /> <br /> The Aesir, Netjer, Tuatha, and Shen are moderates. They nominally believe in the Titanomachy but default to keeping the Titans in-line or assimilating them rather than killing or imprisoning them.<br /> <br /> The Orisha and the Manitou are the doves. Not that the Manitou aren't willing to throw down with their own Titans when they have to, but they don't view it as a great cosmic struggle involving other Pantheons. And the Orisha don't even believe in the god/Titan distinction.<br /> <br /> The Yazata are confused because they are Titanomachy hardliners by inclination, but they thought the Deva were Titans! And the Deva think the same thing about them! So it's hard for them to be involved with the militant camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:06:23-07:00","id":1141748,"title":"","content":"In the World, wouldn't Vedaism (centered on Indra and his generation, with more unambiguous polytheism than Monism) stand as a fourth major form of Hinduism, the same way other ancient religions have continuously survived?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:06:50-07:00","id":1141749,"title":"","content":"Kali will be getting an expanded writeup in the Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:14:22-07:00","id":1141754,"title":"","content":"I rather like this pantheon write-up. My limited exposition to the religions and mythology involved nonwithstanding, it looks inspired. The uniqueness of the first paragraph for each deity addressing their many and sometimes contradicting origins in a hymn was already mentioned, and lends a pretty evocative quality to the whole. In contrast, the current of modernity and contemporary reflection in the text alongside the mythic references has been a charm point in the previewed Scion 2e writing for me, and I'm very fond of it here.<br /> <br /> It's got a number of very amusing and appropriate bits, like Yama being THE MOST OVERWORKED GOD. The portrayal of Lanka and what it's become in the context of this World where all legends are true is also very interesting, and it is wise that it's distanced from Sri Lanka and exists distinctly from it, for obvious reasons that have also already been mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-19-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:21:01-07:00","id":1141756,"title":"","content":"I'd add that the Loa are firmly in the dove category as well. And the Nemetondevos, assuming any of them are alive in 2e, probably have more to concern themselves with than titans, though I could see them going with the Matrones as titans approach as well. I do like the way titans are being handled, and it can make for some good drama within bands when you have pcs with conflicting views on them.<br /> <br /> I fully admit that I need to do a lot more research on the Deva, but I really love that Kartikeya, Durga and Varuna made the cut this time, and that they're playing up the (to me anyway) fascinating connection between the Deva and Yazata. I am curious if the possible Varuna and Ahura Mazda connection will be addressed in companion, and if its even possible for a god to have a primordial for a mantle in another pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T11:45:27-07:00","id":1141829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141748#post1141748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the World, wouldn't Vedaism (centered on Indra and his generation, with more unambiguous polytheism than Monism) stand as a fourth major form of Hinduism, the same way other ancient religions have continuously survived?</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>could</i> do that in individual games, but that poses some unique issues that I think make it difficult to use as a Baseline assumption. Firstly, Vedic era Hinudism (which some also call Shrautism, after Shruti, the collective name of the four Vedas) is significantly different from latter day Puranic era Hinduism... in a way that is not the same as saying that Ancient Greek or Egyptian practices were not large scale overrun by the Abrahamic faiths... in one case, a religion was replaced by another, in another, the religion <i>itself</i> evolved into a different one entirely.<br /> <br /> Secondly, we have the issues with compatibility... Vaishnavism Shaivism and Shaktism might disagree with each other on several points, but they at least have the same general cast of characters... there's no Durga in the Vedas, no Shiva (not as we know him anyway, Rudra exists), no Ganesh or Kartikkeya, a deity named Vishnu who's a Sun God and bears next to no resemblance to the Vishnu of today, a Sarasvati who is only a river Goddess and so on... the Vedic era Gods exist in modern Hindu narratives, but the modern Hindu Gods don't exist in the Vedas.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, you'd have to make them their own Pantheon Path... Duty and Conscience are not Vedic era ideals... a Vedic era Pantheon is likely to have a setup more akin to the Tuatha Honor vs Prowess deal, to represent a culture that simultaneously worships cosmic Order and Truth, and is also a warrior civilization looking for glory in battle. Yoga also doesn't work as a Vedic era PSP since the union with the Supreme Godhead concept doesn't properly get formulated till at least the Upanishads... instead, the Vedic era Gods are much more invested in Sacrifice, to the point where I think you could safely rename the Teotl PSP Sraddha (the Vedic concept of reciprocity between Man and God through sacrifice) and use it as a replacement.<br /> <br /> So yes, you could do it, but about the only way to make it work is to treat the Vedic era Gods as their own Pantheon with the Tuatha Virtues and the Teotl PSP, and have all the Vedic era Gods essentially have a Mantle in both the old Pantheon and the new <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I meant to discuss this earlier but it completely slipped my mind... but I prefer to treat the Puranic Chandra and the Vedic as either separate deities or significantly different Mantles of the same deity... Soma in the Vedas is primarily associated with the Soma plant, with his Lunar associations being a distant second... he IS a Moon God, but that's barely mentioned and/or relevant to the Vedas, which are significantly more interested in the Sun.<br /> <br /> Chandra, on the other hand, is a Moon God first and foremost, and a God of astrology and the calendar... he has minimal associations with Soma, though he came out of the same Churning of the Oceans Episode as Amrita. They are treated as the same God, with Chandra being called Soma and Soma being a byword for Moon, but to be perfectly honest Soma is practically Titanic in the Vedas... concerned only with his Plant self and it's properties and use in sacrifice... which should surprise no one since Soma of the Deva and Haoma of the Ahura are probably the same person (even if the plant they represent might not have been). Chandra by contrast is a lively figure who is a ladies man, being married to the 27 lunar asterisms and carrying on a torrid affair with the wife of Brihaspati, with whom he had the Planet Mercury as a son.<br /> <br /> So yeah, if I were designing it, I'd treat Soma as a Titan of Fertility and Moon, with possibly Deception (for the possible hallucinogenic effects of Soma) and Chandra as a God with Lover, Sage and Healer as Callings, and Moon, Fortune, Order and Health as Purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T16:56:08-07:00","id":1141937,"title":"","content":"Yama is going to become the most overworked god if the Balinese and Burmese pantheons ever shows up.<br /> <br /> Surprised that Burmese names for Ganesha and Saraswati were a part of the write-up. I really want a mainland Southeast Asian group of gods as a sub-pantheon to the Devas.<br /> <br /> I can't really see Brahma as a primordial outside of South Asian contexts. He's worshipped as a god of prosperity and wealth in Thailand. Shrines for him are everywhere. He's on the same tier as Indra and Sri in terms of devotion.<br /> <br /> The preview for the Deva was one of the best write-ups I've read so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:43:52-07:00","id":1141953,"title":"","content":"I will not try to discuss or give my opinion on the Deva Pantheon Update, as I know basically nothing about the Pantheon, but, at least, gave me interest in trying to understand the &quot;whos&quot; and &quot;whats&quot; of the Pantheon. Can someone suggest me a good, but simple and basic, source to learn about it? Maybe a documentary, a book or a film.<br /> <br /> If it has a strong visual component even better, cause it would be easier to picture stuff and I know very little of how this Pantheon should look like (clothing, the otherworlds, weapons, etc.).<br /> <br /> In advance, Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 09-20-2017, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T21:05:11-07:00","id":1142024,"title":"","content":"One thing I love about the more recent pantheon previews is just the sheer density of information they manage to cram in but still have it be easily digestible. I hope some of the older ones got to this level during second draft. After reading them I feel like while I can't have a theological discourse about them I can at least make a character or run a game without completely messing up the ones that I don't already know decently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T21:45:05-07:00","id":1142030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141953#post1141953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will not try to discuss or give my opinion on the Deva Pantheon Update, as I know basically nothing about the Pantheon, but, at least, gave me interest in trying to understand the &quot;whos&quot; and &quot;whats&quot; of the Pantheon. Can someone suggest me a good, but simple and basic, source to learn about it? Maybe a documentary, a book or a film.<br /> <br /> If it has a strong visual component even better, cause it would be easier to picture stuff and I know very little of how this Pantheon should look like (clothing, the otherworlds, weapons, etc.).<br /> <br /> I advance, Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V_NJAJGCKD8\" data-code=\"V_NJAJGCKD8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/V_NJAJGCKD8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That would be a good enough place to start <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sadly there's not a lot of sources on Hinduism (that I know of) that are not either A. Hopelessly incomplete, or B. Coming from too much of an outsider perspective to properly understand it or C.Coming from too much of an insider perspective that it ends up becoming more of a recruitment video than a scholarly source for people wanting to understand the religion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you have any more specific questions, feel free to PM me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd be happy to help either directly or with trying to dredge up some videos or the like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T23:52:42-07:00","id":1142055,"title":"","content":"Also, a thing that amused me.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that ONE of these Pantheon Writeups will be nice enough to reveal that no, don't worry, you haven't been pronouncing like 80% of these names wrong.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I decided on a lark to glance at the Wikipedia page for the Deva's Astra. I figure it'd be a nice summary to kinda get an idea what they're like.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astra_(weapon)\" target=\"_blank\">So even if this isn't the MOST accurate</a>, if it's anywhere near the ballpark... <b>Holy SHIT.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-20-2017, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:05:04-07:00","id":1142113,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a>, I will certainly watch it. I tried to look something up, but my google-fu failed me and I found nothing that looked like a good introduction.<br /> <br /> If I ever have any doubt on this subject, you will be the first I will look after, but I will need to study a lot of it before I even have doubts.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 09-20-2017, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:17:11-07:00","id":1142114,"title":"","content":"So do Scions of Yamaraja (aka Yanluo, aka Emma-O) get to pick which Pantheon Path they follow between Deva, Palas, Shen, and Kami, and wield the PSP tied to their cultural Virtues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:55:16-07:00","id":1142171,"title":"","content":"If you want some fast background on the <i>R\u0101m\u0101ya\u1e47a</i> with evocative \u00e6sthetics, I recommend the picture book <i>Ramayana: the Divine Loophole</i> by Pixar's Sanjay Patel, and Nina Paley's film <i>Sita Sings the Blues.</i> I tried to read Deepak Chopra's <i>R\u0101m\u0101ya\u1e47a</i> comic in a religion class once, but it was too pretentious and annoying so we all gave up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142114#post1142114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do Scions of Yamaraja (aka Yanluo, aka Emma-O) get to pick which Pantheon Path they follow between Deva, Palas, Shen, and Kami, and wield the PSP tied to their cultural Virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:02:01-07:00","id":1142176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142171#post1142171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious,what his forth PSP Yidam,does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:30:34-07:00","id":1142184,"title":"","content":"Who are the Palas, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:42:34-07:00","id":1142189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142184#post1142184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the Palas, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Buddhist Pantheon,i'm almost sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:22:08-07:00","id":1142205,"title":"","content":"I'd guess a Vajrayana one since they have the most distinct set of deities.<br /> <br /> The use of the word &quot;Yidam&quot; backs that up pretty strongly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:26:33-07:00","id":1142207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142189#post1142189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Buddhist Pantheon,i'm almost sure</div> </div> </div> </div>The name of Yamaraja's fourth PSP, Yidam, pretty much confirms he's a member of a Buddhist Pantheon - Yidam is a Buddhist term referring to a type of deity said to be manifestations of Buddhahood or enlightened mind. It's sometimes translated as &quot;tutelary deity&quot; or &quot;meditational deity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given we can match Yamaraja's other three PSPs to other pantheons, it's likely Yidam is the Palas PSP, pointing to them being the Buddhist Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:19:53-07:00","id":1142228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141477#post1141477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Samudra,Remember Rishis storyes you told me? This preview makes them even more awesome,since it means that Brahma,the <i>primordial</i> was turned into a baby by Atri and Cursed by Bhrigu,That's just Awesome in spades</div> </div> </div> </div>Credit where it's due Nicolas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Atri's wife Anusuya is the one who turned the Trimurti into babies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:20:39-07:00","id":1142229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142055#post1142055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a thing that amused me.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that ONE of these Pantheon Writeups will be nice enough to reveal that no, don't worry, you haven't been pronouncing like 80% of these names wrong.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I decided on a lark to glance at the Wikipedia page for the Deva's Astra. I figure it'd be a nice summary to kinda get an idea what they're like.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astra_(weapon)\" target=\"_blank\">So even if this isn't the MOST accurate</a>, if it's anywhere near the ballpark... <b>Holy SHIT.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Gada entry seems spurious to me... Gada is just the term for a mace in Sanskrit and I'm not aware of Hanuman's being in anyway special beyond the fact that he doesn't break it every time he hits something full force.<br /> <br /> Most of the others, however, I'm pretty sure do exist somewhere or the other in the literature... some may be in regional side stories (because the number of people who looked at the Ramayana and Mahabharata and decided 'nope, these aren't long enough' and proceeded to write additional side stories is astounding). Though a minor point... Astra is just the term for a ranged superweapon of mass destruction... the term for a <i>melee</i> superweapon of mass destruction is a Shastra, which would include Vishnu's Kaumodaki and Shiva's Trishula. We just so rarely see Shastras employed that the term Astra has come to mean 'general weapon of mass destruction'... which is mostly a side effect of the fact that only the best and most glorious of warriors get to use Astras, and the best and most glorious of warriors are all archers, since the Hindu mindset considers ranged combat to be significantly more glorious than melee.<br /> <br /> And let's not forget <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> any of those wonderful Astras can be YOURS for the low low price of the Devotion's Reward Boon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:21:38-07:00","id":1142230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142171#post1142171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want some fast background on the <i>R\u0101m\u0101ya\u1e47a</i> with evocative \u00e6sthetics, I recommend the picture book <i>Ramayana: the Divine Loophole</i> by Pixar's Sanjay Patel, and Nina Paley's film <i>Sita Sings the Blues.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sita Sings the Blues is pretty much my favourite adaptation of the Ramayana ever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:22:30-07:00","id":1142233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Svarogg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141937#post1141937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really see Brahma as a primordial outside of South Asian contexts. He's worshipped as a god of prosperity and wealth in Thailand. Shrines for him are everywhere. He's on the same tier as Indra and Sri in terms of devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I think you could homebrew him into a Creator/Sage/Judge with Order, Forge, Fortune and Prosperity as Purviews (he's already got an amazing write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T13:01:38-07:00","id":1142274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142229#post1142229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We just so rarely see Shastras employed that the term Astra has come to mean 'general weapon of mass destruction'... which is mostly a side effect of the fact that only the best and most glorious of warriors get to use Astras, and the best and most glorious of warriors are all archers, since the Hindu mindset considers ranged combat to be significantly more glorious than melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, duly noted.<br /> <br /> I admit reading up on the Astras made me imagine a Deva Scion getting to borrow one to take on a rampaging titanspawn, and admitting to the rest of her band that she needs to aim carefully.<br /> <br /> Because if she misses or messes up, she COULD blow up the entire city.<br /> <br /> (In the scene I imagined, while the others react with appropriate shock, the Teotl Scion jokingly asks if she could take out Los Angeles. Her sense of humor can be hit-or-miss)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T13:58:06-07:00","id":1142293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142228#post1142228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Credit where it's due Nicolas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Atri's wife Anusuya is the one who turned the Trimurti into babies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh oops,sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T01:24:31-07:00","id":1142438,"title":"","content":"I guess I don't understand basic Hindu mythology as much as I thought I did, because I thought Kali was sort of a big deal. Why would she get relegated to the companion (ie, the non-hardcopy piece)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:23:12-07:00","id":1142615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142438#post1142438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I don't understand basic Hindu mythology as much as I thought I did, because I thought Kali was sort of a big deal. Why would she get relegated to the companion (ie, the non-hardcopy piece)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have been BECAUSE Kali is recognizable? I vaguely recall one of the devs saying that Annie X, the iconic Deva Scion, in 1e was a Scion of Kali, but in 2e isn't, because Kali is more-or-less the go-to Hindu goddess in Pop Culture. Let's shake it up a bit.<br /> <br /> And I remember seeing Neall answer the &quot;Why isn't Kali in the Core?&quot; question with &quot;Well we gotta save SOMETHING for the Companion&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm just guessing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:36:33-07:00","id":1142623,"title":"","content":"Guesses on gods in the Companion if there's only be one per Pantheon<br /> <br /> Tuatha: Goibniu<br /> <br /> Theoi: Hecate<br /> <br /> Netjer: Neber-Het<br /> <br /> Orisha: Aganju<br /> <br /> Deva: Kali (confirmed)<br /> <br /> Teotl: Tlazolteotl<br /> <br /> Shen: He Bo is of more importance in historic legend, but Caishen gets more modern worship, so I'd say 50/50 odds on that one<br /> <br /> (we'll see with Kami, Manitou, and Aesir when we get a look at those Pantheons and who gets left out)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:24:04-07:00","id":1142722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142615#post1142615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might have been BECAUSE Kali is recognizable? I vaguely recall one of the devs saying that Annie X, the iconic Deva Scion, in 1e was a Scion of Kali, but in 2e isn't, because Kali is more-or-less the go-to Hindu goddess in Pop Culture. Let's shake it up a bit.<br /> <br /> And I remember seeing Neall answer the &quot;Why isn't Kali in the Core?&quot; question with &quot;Well we gotta save SOMETHING for the Companion&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm just guessing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I can see that as a draw for the companion, but it feels weird to be taking out one of the more popular Devas from the core product and not the other presented pantheons. We'll see I guess - is this sort of logic going to lead to Thor being in the Companion? It seems unlikely, but I also would have assumed Kali would make the cut.<br /> <br /> It just feels like it's shortchanging one of the more vital parts of Hinduism (and I definitely only have a passing acquaintance with Hinduism, so I could be wrong on that point) in place of some less central figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 09-21-2017, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T16:03:09-07:00","id":1142730,"title":"","content":"It could be a balance thing since from what I understand (admittedly not much) doesn't she have a lot of thematic/responsibility overlap with Shiva as far as things like destruction being necessary for creation and such? Or maybe the companion has a something in it that fits her perfectly that they couldn't fit in the main book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T16:47:15-07:00","id":1142747,"title":"","content":"There are already people complaining about the wait for the books.<br /> Me, an EX3 Kickstarter vet: &quot;Oh my sweet summer child&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T19:26:55-07:00","id":1142783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142438#post1142438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I don't understand basic Hindu mythology as much as I thought I did, because I thought Kali was sort of a big deal. Why would she get relegated to the companion (ie, the non-hardcopy piece)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong... She is a very big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142615#post1142615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might have been BECAUSE Kali is recognizable? I vaguely recall one of the devs saying that Annie X, the iconic Deva Scion, in 1e was a Scion of Kali, but in 2e isn't, because Kali is more-or-less the go-to Hindu goddess in Pop Culture. Let's shake it up a bit.<br /> <br /> And I remember seeing Neall answer the &quot;Why isn't Kali in the Core?&quot; question with &quot;Well we gotta save SOMETHING for the Companion&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm just guessing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't aware of Annie getting a new Patron... interesting, I wonder who it is. Also Mendez is the one who said that, earlier in this very thread in fact <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142722#post1142722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I can see that as a draw for the companion, but it feels weird to be taking out one of the more popular Devas from the core product and not the other presented pantheons. We'll see I guess - is this sort of logic going to lead to Thor being in the Companion? It seems unlikely, but I also would have assumed Kali would make the cut.<br /> <br /> It just feels like it's shortchanging one of the more vital parts of Hinduism (and I definitely only have a passing acquaintance with Hinduism, so I could be wrong on that point) in place of some less central figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is one of the things that struck me the most about the write-up, but since Kali is my chosen patron I'm not exactly unbiased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not to detract from my earlier praise of the Preview of course... it is still an excellent and evocative presentation for the Deva as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142730#post1142730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be a balance thing since from what I understand (admittedly not much) doesn't she have a lot of thematic/responsibility overlap with Shiva as far as things like destruction being necessary for creation and such? Or maybe the companion has a something in it that fits her perfectly that they couldn't fit in the main book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kali and Shiva do have thematic overlap, but then the Trimurti and their wives in general always do (though perhaps them more than most). At most I can guess that as Kali as often in myths as much Mantle worn by other Goddesses as Goddess in Her own right, She got pushed to the Companion since that's where the rules for dealing with Mantles as separate Patrons and the such are detailed. That's my best guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:09:06-07:00","id":1142886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142623#post1142623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guesses on gods in the Companion if there's only be one per Pantheon<br /> <br /> Tuatha: Goibniu<br /> <br /> Theoi: Hecate<br /> <br /> Netjer: Neber-Het<br /> <br /> Orisha: Aganju<br /> <br /> Deva: Kali (confirmed)<br /> <br /> Teotl: Tlazolteotl<br /> <br /> Shen: He Bo is of more importance in historic legend, but Caishen gets more modern worship, so I'd say 50/50 odds on that one<br /> <br /> (we'll see with Kami, Manitou, and Aesir when we get a look at those Pantheons and who gets left out)</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, if we're doing this then....<br /> <br /> Deva: Kali<br /> <br /> Netjer: Neber-Het<br /> <br /> Orishas: Erinle<br /> <br /> Shen: Houyi<br /> <br /> Teotl: Tlazolteotl<br /> <br /> Tuatha: Goibhniu<br /> <br /> Theoi: Heracles<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:45:21-07:00","id":1142901,"title":"","content":"Houyi is mentioned in Chang'E's writeup implying that unlike her he didn't achieve godhood and died long ago - but he might be viable for an Incarnate!<br /> <br /> Heracles I'm betting they'll hold back (along with Imhotep) till we see the 2E version of the Keepers of the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-22-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T09:45:16-07:00","id":1142938,"title":"","content":"For the Theoi, maybe we'll see someone like Janus or an Etruscan mantle for one of the 12 primary Olympians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:19:40-07:00","id":1142956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1142938#post1142938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Theoi, maybe we'll see someone like Janus or an Etruscan mantle for one of the 12 primary Olympians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely be down for Janus, I just don't know if they're waiting on doing a full sub-antheon of surviving Sabine gods or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_l