gods, I'm finding 17 to be the magic number for how many to focus on for each Pantheon. So the additional 4 here would be Kali (who we know we're getting), Chandra, Ganga, and Brahma for settings/eras where he is more active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:07:05-07:00","id":1143556,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a>, I've read reference to Agni and Soma (specifically in the lunar role more than the plant, so pretty directly translating to Chandra) being in a sexual relationship. Do you have any familiarity with that tradition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T15:57:49-07:00","id":1143614,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... would Ushas be perhaps an appropriate additional Deva? And I still think Hanuman would be an appropriate divine parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12989,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","user":"Center-of-All","date":". 09-24-2017, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T18:14:59-07:00","id":1143634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1143614#post1143614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... would Ushas be perhaps an appropriate additional Deva? And I still think Hanuman would be an appropriate divine parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>On reread Hanuman is there the same way Rama and Krishna are - as those latter two are avatars Vishnu, so Hanuman is an Avatar of Shiva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T12:04:44-07:00","id":1143858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1143556#post1143556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a>, I've read reference to Agni and Soma (specifically in the lunar role more than the plant, so pretty directly translating to Chandra) being in a sexual relationship. Do you have any familiarity with that tradition?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a passage in the Shatapatha Brahmana that refers to Agni and Soma as a productive pair, but also applies the same name to Indra and Agni, so the exact nature is debatable. I have heard this theory many times, but don't know of any specific source for it (which doesn't mean there isn't one, mind you, as A. I hardly know every piece of Hindu literature there is and B. This is Vedic era myth, which is a somewhat hazy subject to begin with, so I can't give you a definitive answer). However, Vedic era Hindu religion essentialy consists of offerings, primarily of Soma, into Fire, in the hopes of generating wealth, food and progeny... in this context, Soma has been identified with semen, Agni with the womb, and the resulting wealth with the child. This metaphor can be taken literally as well... it is a valid interpretation to say that the Divinities of Soma and Fire are likewise in a sexual relationship.<br /> <br /> However, interestingly, the same passage of the Shatapatha Brahmana <i>does</i> explicitly say that Mitra deposits his seed in Varuna on the new moon night and nature rejoices. Other passages in this or other texts refer to the positions being reversed. I wonder what Varuna thinks of his erstwhile boyfriend being a Yazata now.<br /> <br /> Also interestingly, there are multiple versions of the story of Kartikkeya's birth where Agni swallows Shiva's semen and is either impregnated himself or passes on the seed to another being, so clearly the 'Agni has sex with other guys' theme has staying power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T12:23:00-07:00","id":1143864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1143614#post1143614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... would Ushas be perhaps an appropriate additional Deva? And I still think Hanuman would be an appropriate divine parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ushas and her sister Ratri are both potential God candidates, though Ushas at least in the Vedas gives off a bit of a Titanic vibe... unlike Ratri who is more a Loving Guardian figure who protects against the dangers of the Night, Ushas is a more remote, awe inspiring figure of Light and even more importantly Order, who is often said to 'diminish the days of men'.<br /> <br /> Ushas in the modern day has to some extent been combined with Saranyu, Goddess of the Dawn and Clouds, and wife of Surya. The festival of Chhath explicitly identifies Ushas and Saranyu as one, so like the erstwhile Soma becoming Chandra, the Vedic Ushas may have beome the Puranic Saranyu. Interestingly, Saranyu once created a clone of herself from her shadow... this clone called Chhaya (literally 'Shadow') is a goddess of shadows and darkness and can be seen as a sort of Puranic era Ratri, who sadly has next to no worship in the modern day.<br /> <br /> Hanuman, like all Avatars, <i>could</i> may be treated as a separate God for purposes of patronage (I say patronage and not parenthood since many traditions describe Hanuman as a sworn virgin, so he is unlikely to sire Scions). It can just get very difficult sometimes to decide which figures in Hinduism should be individually written up, and which treated as Mantles or Incarnations of others (I mean, depending on whom you ask, Brahma Vishnu and Shiva are all Mantles of the same Primordial deity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T20:20:51-07:00","id":1144616,"title":"","content":"So... were Dyaus and Prithvi Primordials who no one has heard from in millennia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T22:26:07-07:00","id":1144636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1144616#post1144616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... were Dyaus and Prithvi Primordials who no one has heard from in millennia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dyaus and Prithvi, along with the third member of the Vedic Triad Aditi, are most definitely Primordials... or at least they were in the Vedas.<br /> <br /> Unlike the more complicated 14 + 2 Plane cosmology of the Puranic era, the Vedas saw all of reality divided into a much simpler 3 Tier system : Heaven (Svar), Earth (Bhu) and everything In-Between (Bhuvar). These three Goddesses (Yes, <b>three</b> god<i>esses</i>, I'm getting to that) are the Primordial personifications of these three Planes. Dyaus (Shining One) is the Embodiment of Heaven, whose Principal deity is the Sun and who is the abode of the Gods; Aditi (Unbound One), is the Embodiment of In-Between, whose Principal Deity is Indra/Vayu and who is the abode of the blessed ancestors; Prithvi (Vast One) is the Embodiment of Earth, whose Principal deity is Agni and who is the abode of humans.<br /> <br /> While Dyaus probably originally was a Sky <i>Father</i> in the far away mists of time, their gender appears significantly ambiguous in the Veda, which do call Heaven and Earth the parents of all things, but also refer to the sisterhood of Heaven and Earth. Texts that provide commentary and additions to the Vedas often consider Dyaus a female divinity. The Taittritya Brahmana, which has an entire section dedicated to worshiping goddesses, mentions Dyaus as the very first Goddess on that list. So, for symmetry's sake, I always prefer to take Dyaus as a Goddess, Mother Heaven. Sadly, Dyaus is pretty much non-existent in modern day Hindu worship... already in the Veda Indra was taking over much of her role, and there's basically no Dyaus worship today.<br /> <br /> Prithvi is an interesting case... her importance in the Veda seems greater than Dyaus' by a fair margin (Dyaus has no independant hymns, she is worsipped only as a pair with Pritvi, whearas Prithvi has a few hymns where she <i>is</i> worshipped alone). The Puranas introduced BhuDevi (literally, Earth Goddess) who is the principal earth deity, but there's a lot of back and forth on whether BhuDevi is the God form of the Primordial Prithvi, or a Mantle of Lakshmi, who is also hymned as BhuDevi... the latter tradition seems to have come out both as a way to maintain Trimurti and Tridevi ascendance over the old Vedic Gods, by literally making one of them merely an aspect of Lakshmi, and a way to get around the awkwardness of the myths where Vishnu's Varaha Incarnation has sex with BhuDevi (if she's an Incarnation of Vishnu's wife, then that doesn't count as cheating, which is a big deal in Hinduism, where faithfulness to your partner is a very big deal in most traditions). This does of course get kinda weird in the Ramayana where Queen Sita, another Incarnation of Lakshmi, is born as a daughter of Bhudevi/Prithvi, but I guess even the Gods can't keep all their Incarnations straight sometimes. Whichever version you decide to go with though, Prithvi does get a modicum of worship and respect and mentions in myth so she's arguably doing the best of the three.<br /> <br /> Aditi has possibly had the greatest fall of the three... at least Dyaus got away with just becoming obscure. Aditi in the Veda is the Goddess of Unbound Infinity, whose Infinite Might keeps the Worlds in Order... she is perhaps the earliest conception of what would later become Shakti. Aditi is Indra's mother in the Veda, as well as Varuna's and sometimes even Vishnu's and Mitra's and a host of other deities who are collectively identified as the Adityas, the Sons of Aditi... all, especially Indra, are implied to gain their phenomenal cosmic powers by virtue of Aditi... Indra is said to have become mighty as an infant by drinking her milk. One hymn in the Veda even declares:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Aditi is Heaven, Aditi is In-Between, Aditi is the Mother, the Father, and the Child... Aditi is verily All the Universal Gods, Aditi is the Five Classes of Men... All who have been born are Aditi, All who will be born are nought but Aditi&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That declaration has similarities to Durga's pronouncement in the Devi Mahatmyam, where She states &quot;I alone move throughout the Universe... Who Else is there but Me?&quot; and indeed Durga is called Aditi and Devamata (Mother of the Gods) due to her Unbound Power and Motherly Functions. Unfortunately, the actual Aditi got downgraded <i>severely</i> into one of the wives of the Sage Rishi Kashyapa, and while she's still mother of Indra and the Vedic Devas, basically ends up portrayed as a meek housewife figure, where the Primordial Aditi had no male counterpart, and indeed had no need of such.<br /> <br /> So Yeah, the Shining One, the Unbound One and the Vast One definitely were Primordials at some point... what they are now depends on which version you want to go with (Personally I prefer to leave all three of them as Primordials, and treat Bhudevi as a shared Mantle between Prithvi and Lakshmi and basically assume the Primordial Aditi either became Durga at some point or became the Primordial Shakti of whom Durga (and all Goddesses) are a part).<br /> <br /> (That was probably way more info than you were looking for, but I'll take any chance I can get to talk about Aditi who is one of my favourite 'Why does no one talk about her!' figures ever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:44:47-07:00","id":1144991,"title":"","content":"This is actually really interesting since I first heard of Dyaus via researching origins of Zeus (I was looking for an archaic name for a likely same god to use as a company name in my Scion game) and found Dyeus existing as some kind of Indo-European skyfather type deity which Zeus is likely a line of descent from in terms of identity, but is also likely Dyaus and possibly Dionysus. I didn't know much about Dyaus since I didn't click THAT wiki link at the time (namely, scrambling to find a neat name during a session for something I really should have named beforehand) but your post is, as it always is, extremely informative.<br /> <br /> In the World, I wonder if there's some way to link the two pantheons via that Dyeus connection which isn't totally terrible writing. I'm half wondering if maybe, as Durga might be the goddess who was once the primordial Shakti who was once the primordial Aditi in your framing there, maybe Zeus has some complex relationship with Dyaus. I doubt he actually is them, since he is also the child of named Titans in myth and this is Scion, but hey maybe they can both be impossibly true. Or Dyeus is what Zeus was before becoming a god vs. primordial. Or something else. <br /> <br /> I just feel like there's some weird ideas to mine there for a game to throw Theoi players for a trip at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T21:38:49-07:00","id":1145093,"title":"","content":"Primordial: Proto-Indo-European","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T05:03:28-07:00","id":1145170,"title":"","content":"It manifests as a very awe inspiring cloud and neither speaks nor acts in the modern world. Perhaps it is just a cloud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T06:50:25-07:00","id":1151294,"title":"","content":"the preview states Vishnu is the leader of Devas,surpassing Indra,although the Indra doesn't technically agrees.<br /> Are there any tales where Indra fights with Vishnu over something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T10:55:04-07:00","id":1151392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1151294#post1151294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the preview states Vishnu is the leader of Devas,surpassing Indra,although the Indra doesn't technically agrees.<br /> Are there any tales where Indra fights with Vishnu over something?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'll get your question about opposition out of the way first... In general, Indra does not oppose Vishnu in myth. In the Vedas, Vishnu is a minor Sun god possibly representing the Sun's power as keeper of Time and in some versions of the Vritra myth he helps Indra to kill Vritra (in some others Sarasvati does, so both a future Trimurti and a future Tridevi member have a story of helping Indra in his great battle against Vritra in the Veda). In latter day Puranic era myth, we see Indra actually becoming Vishnu's supplicant... Indra comes to Vishnu after the demon of the week has taken over Svarga and asks him for help and Vishnu usually does, often by taking on an Avatara.<br /> <br /> However, while Indra doesn't get into fights with Vishnu, he <i>does</i> get into not one but two scrapes with Krishna, Vihsnu's most popular Avatara. In one story, during the rainy season, the inhabitants of Krishna's village get together to worship Indra... Krishna, then just a child, argues that they should worship the nearby mountain Govardhan instead as it is the mountain that stops the clouds, causing the rain. The villagers agree... Indra is furious at this and attacks the village, causing torrential rainstorms. To protect the people, Krishna picks up the mountain with his little finger, keeping it aloft with that one single finger of one hand, while the entire village takes shelter underneath the mountain. He also plays the flute one-handed while he's doing this cuz Krishna just likes to show-off sometimes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Indra admits defeat and apologizes to Krishna.<br /> <br /> In another story many years later, Agni approaches a now adult Krishna and his friend Arjuna, Scion of Indra himself, and says that he wishes to eat the Khandava forest (i.e. burn it down) but he can't as Indra himself protects the place. In return for Arjuna's protection while he eats, Agni gives him the Gandiva bow, forged by Brahma himself and a match for Vishnu's Sharanga and Shiva's Pinaka bows, along with two quivers of infinite arrows. Agni starts to burn the forest down, and Indra turns up with many other Deva to battle him, but is fought to a standstill by his son and Krihsna until a Divine Voice tells him to just give up already, which he does.<br /> <br /> That question being answered, I want to tackle another question... that of Deva leadership. It's a funny thing that while Indra is the top God of the Vedas, I hesitate to call him the King of the Vedic era Gods, not because he isn't the most powerful, but because calling him king implies that he <i>rules</i> them, and no one really rules the Vedic Gods... in the Vedas the Gods are mostly independent and rarely if ever interfere with each other... they roam throughout the World, attending sacrifices, abiding in the Fire and Wind, in Sun and Soma, in Thunder and Sea. Indra is the most honoured and mightiest among them, but he can't be bothered sitting on a throne all day making policy or passing Judgement... in the Vedic era Virtue set of Honor and Prowess that I mentioned earlier, Indra is the epitome of Prowess... Varuna is the Epitome of Honor, and in his time as ruler he probably did hold court, but that is so long ago that we have next to records of what Hinduism was even like back then.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, it's the Puranic era that actually makes Indra a proper 'King' with a court at Amaravati in Svarga and the like... but it was also the Puranic era that decided that 'King' is not top job in the Hindu Pantheon. The Trimurti and Tridevi all outrank Indra, even though he is King. It's just that, the two triads rarely if ever interfere in the day to day workings of Heaven or Earth. The Trimurti and Tridevi work on a cosmic scale, keeping the universe going through it's eternal cycle... for everyday things like the rainy season hitting on time, or sunup or sundown not being interrupted, or the everyday death of living things happens, the Vedic era Gods still answer to Indra. Sure, the Trimurti and Tridevi <i>could</i> interfere and micromanage the day to day running of the universe, but why would they? The Vedic era Gods have been the caretakers of Nature for eons at this point... they know how to do their jobs, and do it well. The two Triads would have been stupid to try and insert themselves into that system and mess it up, so they just placed themselves above it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, tl;dr Indra is still officially king of the Gods, but the Trimurti and Tridevi outrank him, he's still in charge of the Nature Gods of the Veda and keeps the everyday natural world running on schedule, while the two Triads usually work on a more cosmic scale and interfere only as and when necessary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T11:39:20-07:00","id":1151406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1151392#post1151392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I'll get your question about opposition out of the way first... In general, Indra does not oppose Vishnu in myth. In the Vedas, Vishnu is a minor Sun god possibly representing the Sun's power as keeper of Time and in some versions of the Vritra myth he helps Indra to kill Vritra (in some others Sarasvati does, so both a future Trimurti and a future Tridevi member have a story of helping Indra in his great battle against Vritra in the Veda). In latter day Puranic era myth, we see Indra actually becoming Vishnu's supplicant... Indra comes to Vishnu after the demon of the week has taken over Svarga and asks him for help and Vishnu usually does, often by taking on an Avatara.<br /> <br /> However, while Indra doesn't get into fights with Vishnu, he <i>does</i> get into not one but two scrapes with Krishna, Vihsnu's most popular Avatara. In one story, during the rainy season, the inhabitants of Krishna's village get together to worship Indra... Krishna, then just a child, argues that they should worship the nearby mountain Govardhan instead as it is the mountain that stops the clouds, causing the rain. The villagers agree... Indra is furious at this and attacks the village, causing torrential rainstorms. To protect the people, Krishna picks up the mountain with his little finger, keeping it aloft with that one single finger of one hand, while the entire village takes shelter underneath the mountain. He also plays the flute one-handed while he's doing this cuz Krishna just likes to show-off sometimes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Indra admits defeat and apologizes to Krishna.<br /> <br /> In another story many years later, Agni approaches a now adult Krishna and his friend Arjuna, Scion of Indra himself, and says that he wishes to eat the Khandava forest (i.e. burn it down) but he can't as Indra himself protects the place. In return for Arjuna's protection while he eats, Agni gives him the Gandiva bow, forged by Brahma himself and a match for Vishnu's Sharanga and Shiva's Pinaka bows, along with two quivers of infinite arrows. Agni starts to burn the forest down, and Indra turns up with many other Deva to battle him, but is fought to a standstill by his son and Krihsna until a Divine Voice tells him to just give up already, which he does.<br /> <br /> That question being answered, I want to tackle another question... that of Deva leadership. It's a funny thing that while Indra is the top God of the Vedas, I hesitate to call him the King of the Vedic era Gods, not because he isn't the most powerful, but because calling him king implies that he <i>rules</i> them, and no one really rules the Vedic Gods... in the Vedas the Gods are mostly independent and rarely if ever interfere with each other... they roam throughout the World, attending sacrifices, abiding in the Fire and Wind, in Sun and Soma, in Thunder and Sea. Indra is the most honoured and mightiest among them, but he can't be bothered sitting on a throne all day making policy or passing Judgement... in the Vedic era Virtue set of Honor and Prowess that I mentioned earlier, Indra is the epitome of Prowess... Varuna is the Epitome of Honor, and in his time as ruler he probably did hold court, but that is so long ago that we have next to records of what Hinduism was even like back then.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, it's the Puranic era that actually makes Indra a proper 'King' with a court at Amafravati in Svarga and the like... but it was also the Puranic era that decided that 'King' is not top job in the Hindu Pantheon. The Trimurti and Tridevi all outrank Indra, even though he is King. It's just that, the two triads rarely if ever interfere in the day to day workings of Heaven or Earth. The Trimurti and Tridevi work on a cosmic scale, keeping the universe going through it's eternal cycle... for everyday things like the rainy season hitting on time, or sunup or sundown not being interrupted, or the everyday death of living things happens, the Vedic era Gods still answer to Indra. Sure, the Trimurti and Tridevi <i>could</i> interfere and micromanage the day to day running of the universe, but why would they? The Vedic era Gods have been the caretakers of Nature for eons at this point... they know how to do their jobs, and do it well. The two Triads would have been stupid to try and insert themselves into that system and mess it up, so they just placed themselves above it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, tl;dr Indra is still officially king of the Gods, but the Trimurti and Tridevi outrank him, he's still in charge of the Nature Gods of the Veda and keeps the everyday natural world running on schedule, while the two Triads usually work on a more cosmic scale and interfere only as and when necessary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating! I think I'll read the Rig Veda to check out those guys awesomeness firsthand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T15:51:02-07:00","id":1151775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Svarogg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1141937#post1141937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really see Brahma as a primordial outside of South Asian contexts. He's worshipped as a god of prosperity and wealth in Thailand. Shrines for him are everywhere. He's on the same tier as Indra and Sri in terms of devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might turn out he's active as one of the Palas in that context. He is one of the Dharmapalas after all. Perhaps his disappearance into the background in modern Hinduism in India corresponds to him personally adopting the Eight Fold Path and aligning more and more with the Palas rather than the Deva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-21-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T20:50:05-07:00","id":1152689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1145093#post1145093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial: Proto-Indo-European</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I'm misunderstanding but I like to think this is the announcement that the whole language of PIE is a Primordial, probably of Epic Intelligence since that's what you need to wring a whole picture out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T21:15:10-07:00","id":1152703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1152689#post1152689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I'm misunderstanding but I like to think this is the announcement that the whole language of PIE is a Primordial, probably of Epic Intelligence since that's what you need to wring a whole picture out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8310_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8310\" data-vbnamecard=\"8310\">Lula</a> meant is that Dyaus and Prithvi were Primordials from the PIE era, as the great Sky Father and Earth Mother pair. Also a Titan of Language in 2e would probably be a Titan of Artistry, since Epic Intelligence no longer exists. Though the idea of a living Language Primordial that defines a lot of the Indo European Pantheons by it's very existence is actually very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T23:05:49-07:00","id":1152719,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was joking that the ur-language itself was a Primordial &lt;_&lt; but Dyaus and Prithvi as Primordials sounds cool too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T17:19:51-08:00","id":1156195,"title":"","content":"Not that Wikipedia is necessarily a good source, but the article it has on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daeva\" target=\"_blank\">Daevas</a> basically calls bullshit a bit on the Devas X Yazatas thing, claiming that &quot;The once-widespread notion that the radically different functions of Iranian <i>daeva</i> and Indic <i>deva</i> (and <i>ahura </i>versus <i>asura</i>) represented a prehistoric inversion of roles is no longer followed in 21st century academic discourse&quot;. Anyone more informed on this than me care to comment?<br /> <br /> Even <b>if</b> the whole situation is indeed more of a product of old conjectures than factual information, I still think it is too much of a good set-up to pass up on for the game, though I wonder if the relatively few remaining worshipers of the Yazatas and the massive following of the Devas might not like it as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T17:48:32-08:00","id":1156202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156195#post1156195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that Wikipedia is necessarily a good source, but the article it has on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daeva\" target=\"_blank\">Daevas</a> basically calls bullshit a bit on the Devas X Yazatas thing, claiming that &quot;The once-widespread notion that the radically different functions of Iranian <i>daeva</i> and Indic <i>deva</i> (and <i>ahura </i>versus <i>asura</i>) represented a prehistoric inversion of roles is no longer followed in 21st century academic discourse&quot;. Anyone more informed on this than me care to comment?<br /> <br /> Even <b>if</b> the whole situation is indeed more of a product of old conjectures than factual information, I still think it is too much of a good set-up to pass up on for the game, though I wonder if the relatively few remaining worshipers of the Yazatas and the massive following of the Devas might not like it as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just took a quick glance through the article, whoever wrote that section should be tisk-tisked for poor citation skills. Whoever edited that in has not footnoted their claims properly, first passing you down to the &quot;In Comparison With Vedic Usage,&quot; section for further information. There they make the statement that the works of this Nyberg, Jacques Duchesne-Guillemin, and Widengren are flawed, immediately fail to provide a citation for a direct quotation, and pass you on to a <i>third</i> sub section for the explanation we were promised at the start of the article, and then this final section totally fails to discuss the promised material. Or potentially I lack the vocabulary to properly 'get' what they saying in the, &quot;In the Younger Avesta,&quot; section.<br /> <br /> Here, I will ping <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar17311_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17311\" data-vbnamecard=\"17311\">xhepablo</a>, this is their field. They might be able to clear this up.The citations on that section are so.... weird. They should have cited that direct quotation, and should have been citing their claims that the works of those previous authors had been dismissed. As well as actually listing the &quot;interminable and entirely conjectural discussions,&quot; that were apparently used to establish the connections. <br /> <br /> Either way, good find Danelsan. It's odd, wonder if someone got in there and fiddled for their own personal beliefs or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T19:14:41-08:00","id":1156221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156202#post1156202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, good find Danelsan. It's odd, wonder if someone got in there and fiddled for their own personal beliefs or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>One time I looked up the Wikipedia page for psychology. Someone had placed it as being related to Satanism and claimed that a psychology degree in the US required reading Mein Kampf. Reported THAT to a moderator, let me tell you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T19:34:45-08:00","id":1156223,"title":"","content":"I wonder what Purview Vritra embodied. I suppose he could have been a &quot;Water&quot; Titan and its just that his powers played out in the restriction of water, which were then unleashed in his slaying. Now other Purview would seem to handle being an embodiment of drought and deprivation better.<br /> <br /> If Hiranyakashipu were to return, he'd make for an interesting Titan of &quot;Prosperity&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think who would make a good currently active Titan or bound Titan in Indian lore, and not coming up with a lot of options since Indra, Durga, and various Avatars of Vishnu are pretty good about knocking them off whenever they rear their heads, so any deity-level Asura threats are either going to be dead ones returning in new Incarnations, or entirely new beings claiming descent from the named ones of legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T10:13:32-08:00","id":1156384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156223#post1156223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what Purview Vritra embodied. I suppose he could have been a &quot;Water&quot; Titan and its just that his powers played out in the restriction of water, which were then unleashed in his slaying. Now other Purview would seem to handle being an embodiment of drought and deprivation better.</div> </div> </div> </div>He might also be a Sky Titan... he may represent the dark sinuous storm clouds that are carved open by Indra's lightning to release the rain that he's hoarding. Also, in the Vedic era, Vritra's battle with Indra is not a one off event... it happens every year during the monsoons, or in some way every time it rains... which both makes Vritra a still existing (or at least constantly reincarnating) Titan, and also an excellent example of the Adversary Calling in your other Thread.<br /> <br /> By the Puranic era Vritra is a one off Asura who steals the waters of the world and is killed by Indra, but only after the latter gets the gift of the Thunderbolt from a Rishi... there's also traditions that say that Vritra was a Brahmin and killing him was a sin that Indra had to undergo multiple trials to atone for... the Vedic era Indra would find all these points kinda ludicrous... Vritra is the stormcloud dragon, not a Brahmin Asura, the idea that the Thunderbolt is something Indra needs to be <i>given</i> is laughable to Vedic Indra whose Thunderbolt is his birthright and either was always his or at best was given to him by his mother Aditi, and the very idea that killing Vritra might be a <i>bad</i> thing would probably make Vedic era Hindus scratch their heads and tell you to lay off the Soma.<br /> <br /> Funnily, there <i>is</i> an actual drought demon in Puranic era myth... Durgamasura, who steals the Vedas from Brahma and uses their power to stop all rainfall... Durga manifests herself as Shatakshi, the Hundred-Eyed One, and cries tears of freshwater to restore the waters to the land, before killing Durgamasura (for those wondering about the name similarity, Dur means difficult or impossible, ga means to go... the word Durga therefore literally means 'You Cannot Go Beyond Her', a fitting name for THE Guardian Goddess... Durgam, from the same root, literally means a difficult time, usually a drought or famine, so Durgamasura's name is basically Drought or Famine Titan).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156223#post1156223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Hiranyakashipu were to return, he'd make for an interesting Titan of &quot;Prosperity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... what makes you think of Prosperity for him? Besides his name literally meaning Golden Hair. I'd have pegged it more to his grandson Bali.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156223#post1156223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think who would make a good currently active Titan or bound Titan in Indian lore, and not coming up with a lot of options since Indra, Durga, and various Avatars of Vishnu are pretty good about knocking them off whenever they rear their heads, so any deity-level Asura threats are either going to be dead ones returning in new Incarnations, or entirely new beings claiming descent from the named ones of legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Deity level Titanic beings in Hindu myth still extant... they're just not very antagonistic. The Titan Bali who conquered Heaven and Earth is still around... after Vishnu in his dwarf Incarnation took them both away from him, he gave him dominion over an entire plane of existence... Sutala, one of the lower levels and a paradise that put Indra's Svarga to shame... Vishnu himself guards Sutala from all threats, and Bali is his dedicated devotee. I'd peg Bali as a Prosperity Titan.<br /> <br /> There's also Mayasura, the Asura architect and master illusionist, responsible for many wonders... he is a Shiva devotee by most counts and also rules an entire plane of existence, Talatala, a realm filled with wondrous artifacts and dazzling illusions... and no way to tell which is which <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mayasura is a Forge/Deception Titan... in fact he's arguably the Titan who's entire expression of either Purview is the other Purview, representing the blurring of lines between artifice and illusion.<br /> <br /> Then of course there are the actual Deities... Vedic era Deva like Soma and Ushas are Titans in my headcanon, though they probably spend most of their time nowadays in their God Mantles of Chandra and Sanjana/Prabha. The Vedic Goddess of Forests Aranyani might also qualify as a Wild Titan, though I can see her as a Goddess as well. The Cosmic serpent Ananta Shesha might also count as an Order Titan but he's probably a Primordial.<br /> <br /> Actually... hold your vahanas... there is ONE example I can think of of a Titan in Hindu myth who's still around... Rahu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, the Darkness Titan responsible for eclipses... he's literally immortal, having tasted Amrita, and continues to assault the Sun and Moon. So there's one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit : Now that I think about it more, there are a few more Titan possibilities... Nirriti, from the Vedas is an option, as a Titan of Death and Misfortune. She's a character that probably gets more attention than is warranted, given her extremely minor presence and very few mentions (the hymn that is usually touted as her hymn in the Rig Veda is actually a hymn to various other divinities to get rid of her) but she's as good a choice as any (given, as you noted, how slim the pickings are for Hindu Titans still active).<br /> <br /> The other options are Diti and Danu, the Mother of the Daitya and Danava clans of Asuras respectively (Which literally mean children of Diti and children of Danu respectively). Diti seems to have associations with the Earth, and her child Hiranyaksha literally steals the Earth and takes it under the sea, while Danu is associated with Water and is mother to Vritra. Which means, interestingly enough, that both these Titans of Earth and water seem obsessed with having their children take away their Purviews from the World rather than spread it out more. Wonder if that's a potential Titan Calling? Also have to wonder what the Deva think of the Tuatha and their whole 'being children of Danu' business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 11-06-2017, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:12:46-08:00","id":1156738,"title":"","content":"There is, by the way, one more potential Deva Antagonist, who is active... only he's really more of a God than a Titan : Shukra, God of the Planet Venus and Guru of the Asura, their Teacher and Preceptor, the counterpart to Brihaspati, God of the Planet Jupiter and Guru of the Deva. Shukra is famous for having acquired the Sanjeevani Mantra from Shiva, a mystic chant that can bring the dead back to life. Some say it was the Asuras compensation for the Deva having taken all the Amrita after the churning of the ocean, though Shukra pretty much never actually uses it in Myth out of respect for Shiva. He is constantly advising the Asura in their attempts to overthrow Indra and his court though, and he is still around, grooming the next generation of Titan spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:16:22-08:00","id":1156740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156738#post1156738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is, by the way, one more potential Deva Antagonist, who is active... only he's really more of a God than a Titan : Shukra, God of the Planet Venus and Guru of the Asura, their Teacher and Preceptor, the counterpart to Brihaspati, God of the Planet Jupiter and Guru of the Deva. Shukra is famous for having acquired the Sanjeevani Mantra from Shiva, a mystic chant that can bring the dead back to life. Some say it was the Asuras compensation for the Deva having taken all the Amrita after the churning of the ocean, though Shukra pretty much never actually uses it in Myth out of respect for Shiva. He is constantly advising the Asura in their attempts to overthrow Indra and his court though, and he is still around, grooming the next generation of Titan spawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>What purviews woud you assign to him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:24:39-08:00","id":1156741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156740#post1156740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What purviews woud you assign to him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Callings : Healer, Leader, Sage<br /> <br /> Purviews : Artistry (Music, Painting), Death, Deception, Health, Passion, Prosperity<br /> <br /> Mind you, other than Death Health and Deception all the others come from his Astrological connections, not mythical ones, so if you want you can cut them down to just those three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:44:09-08:00","id":1156770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156741#post1156741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Callings : Healer, Leader, Sage<br /> <br /> Purviews : Artistry (Music, Painting), Death, Deception, Health, Passion, Prosperity<br /> <br /> Mind you, other than Death Health and Deception all the others come from his Astrological connections, not mythical ones, so if you want you can cut them down to just those three.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if he shares Venus with aphrodite or If the planet exist in more than one plane of existence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T13:27:32-08:00","id":1156779,"title":"","content":"It's a big planet, lots of gods have estates there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T17:42:54-08:00","id":1157840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1156202#post1156202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just took a quick glance through the article, whoever wrote that section should be tisk-tisked for poor citation skills. Whoever edited that in has not footnoted their claims properly, first passing you down to the &quot;In Comparison With Vedic Usage,&quot; section for further information. There they make the statement that the works of this Nyberg, Jacques Duchesne-Guillemin, and Widengren are flawed, immediately fail to provide a citation for a direct quotation, and pass you on to a <i>third</i> sub section for the explanation we were promised at the start of the article, and then this final section totally fails to discuss the promised material. Or potentially I lack the vocabulary to properly 'get' what they saying in the, &quot;In the Younger Avesta,&quot; section.<br /> <br /> Here, I will ping <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar17311_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17311\" data-vbnamecard=\"17311\">xhepablo</a>, this is their field. They might be able to clear this up.The citations on that section are so.... weird. They should have cited that direct quotation, and should have been citing their claims that the works of those previous authors had been dismissed. As well as actually listing the &quot;interminable and entirely conjectural discussions,&quot; that were apparently used to establish the connections.<br /> <br /> Either way, good find Danelsan. It's odd, wonder if someone got in there and fiddled for their own personal beliefs or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you need clarification on, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>? Glad to help in any way I can!<br /> <br /> If you're asking if scholars believe Daevas = Devas, no, definitely not anymore. That's viewed as outdated conjecture really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T17:48:13-08:00","id":1157841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1157840#post1157840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you need clarification on, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>? Glad to help in any way I can!<br /> <br /> If you're asking if scholars believe Daevas = Devas, no, definitely not anymore. That's viewed as outdated conjecture really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Neat! You are absolutely correct in that case <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar868_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"868\" data-vbnamecard=\"868\">danelsan</a>! <br /> <br /> What is counted against it Xhepablo? Is it a timeline issue, that the chronology doesn't sync up in a way that makes it possible? Or something else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T20:52:13-08:00","id":1157866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1157841#post1157841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Neat! You are absolutely correct in that case <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar868_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"868\" data-vbnamecard=\"868\">danelsan</a>!<br /> <br /> What is counted against it Xhepablo? Is it a timeline issue, that the chronology doesn't sync up in a way that makes it possible? Or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be mostly chalked up to a case of &quot;similar, yet vastly different&quot;. While the etymology may be similar and share a source with each other, it's mostly thought in academia that the Vedic Devas were culturally and metaphysically different from the Iranic Daevas, even far before Zoroastrianism. So, we may perceive it as cross-over, but it is far more likely that the condemned Daevas bear very little resemblance to the Devas venerated within Vedic practice besides perhaps some similar nomenclatures and aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T22:47:39-08:00","id":1157880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1141469-september-update-check-out-the-devas?p=1157866#post1157866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be mostly chalked up to a case of &quot;similar, yet vastly different&quot;. While the etymology may be similar and share a source with each other, it's mostly thought in academia that the Vedic Devas were culturally and metaphysically different from the Iranic Daevas, even far before Zoroastrianism. So, we may perceive it as cross-over, but it is far more likely that the condemned Daevas bear very little resemblance to the Devas venerated within Vedic practice besides perhaps some similar nomenclatures and aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Okay, I can totally follow that, sounds similar to the Bealtaine /=/ Irish Ba'al Worship situation you get in Celtic academia at one point. Similarities in names alone isn't a good foundation for a theory, especially when it's being contradicted by a bunch of more ironclad evidence, such as actual cosmological function. That's really neat, thanks very much for enlightening us Xhepablo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/